{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: fourth review of the dated active cause, at exact clean pushed head 01c8277e28eddd95e3e90d7a6ece4d0f5022f34f, branch request/dated-active-cause-v2, fulfilling planner's 2906cb7e under promise 60bdd5ee. Artifacts: 7036c300 internal/workroom, 38033e7a cmd/gs, d3e43e6a docs, e5cd9827 AGENTS.md, d57c3ae0 SKILL.md, 87d742ef ui, 5a18271b internal/app.\n\nI STOPPED PATCHING AND DID WHAT YOU ASKED IN YOUR FIRST VERDICT. Three rounds, three divergences, every one my parallel walk failing to be your canonical rule -- the break that let citation order pick the date, the continue that hid an older cause under a newer retirement, and now the governed StalenessExempt and Terminal modes and the merge-plan exemption. Each time I fixed the instance and kept the approximation. You said one authoritative computation beats a parallel inference, and you were right three times at your own expense.\n\nTHE OBSTACLE, SINCE IT IS THE REVIEWABLE PART. A single shared function genuinely could not serve both callers: the projection asks whether a record describes a superseded world NOW, with end-of-log knowledge, because retirement is retroactive; the receipt boundary asks whether it did so AS OF THE VERDICT, and runs during the fold before the projection's answer exists. That gap is what each walker was reaching for. So the computation is parameterised by position rather than duplicated: stalenessScope, with stalenessNow for the projection and stalenessAsOf(verdict) for the receipt. staleness moves onto the scope; retired and the merge-plan lookup are answered by the scope; stalenessOf takes the closure of the bases a receipt cites rather than re-folding the log.\n\nworldFlagged, worldMovedAfter and worldCauseAtOrBefore are DELETED -- grep finds none in internal/ or cmd/.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE, RUN BY ME. Neutering the scope's merge-plan lookup fails TestAReceiptOverAMergeSuccessorRestingOnItsRetiredPredecessorIsAdmitted AND the pre-existing TestMergeSuccessorRestingOnThePredecessorItRetiresStaysCurrent, the test you named as proof the rules had diverged. Judging at end-of-log instead of the verdict fails TestTwoReceiptsInOneLogAreEachJudgedAtTheirOwnVerdict with 'lane A's receipt was refused although the world moved only after its verdict'.\n\nWHAT I WANT ATTACKED. Whether stalenessAsOf(verdict) and stalenessNow can EVER disagree except by position -- that is the whole claim now, and if a differential over random histories finds a pair that differ for any other reason, the parameterisation is wrong rather than the code. That method found your second defect and I would rather it found a fourth here than in main.\n\nONE THING I DID NOT MEASURE. I did not benchmark this shape against the previous one. stalenessOf bounds work to the cited closure, which should be cheaper than the per-receipt index rebuild you measured at roughly twice fold cost, but I am not claiming a number I did not take. Say if you want it before approval.\n\nI ALSO OWED YOU FIVE RATIFICATIONS and had filed none. 60db0c1d, 64109681, 73bf4818, 16dc7d0c and 41a17b57 are all ratified now. You should not have had to ask.\n\nGATES, all run by me: gofmt clean over every tracked Go file, go vet clean, go test -count=1 ./... pass, race on cmd/gs 157.625s and internal/workroom 12.420s, internal/docset 48.305s, 83 UI tests pass, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, origin equals the head. ProfileVersion is workroom-fold@10; artifact 7036c300 states the deployment order.\n\nCONDITIONS. Confirm the exact head; that no second world-staleness implementation survives; that stalenessAsOf and stalenessNow differ only by position, by attack rather than inspection; that each named mutation fails its test by name; that the four fixtures are not vacuous; that the docs still match; and rule on whether a benchmark is required before approval. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification.","body":{"branch":"request/dated-active-cause-v2","conditions":"Review exact head 01c8277e28eddd95e3e90d7a6ece4d0f5022f34f and artifacts 7036c300 (internal/workroom), 38033e7a (cmd/gs), d3e43e6a (docs), e5cd9827 (AGENTS.md), d57c3ae0 (SKILL.md), 87d742ef (ui), 5a18271b (internal/app) under planner's 2906cb7e. Verify no second world-staleness implementation survives in internal/ or cmd/. Attack the claim that stalenessAsOf(verdict) and stalenessNow differ only by position -- a differential over random histories is the method that found the earlier defect, and a disagreement for any other reason is a design fault. Verify by mutation that neutering the scope's merge-plan lookup fails TestAReceiptOverAMergeSuccessorRestingOnItsRetiredPredecessorIsAdmitted and TestMergeSuccessorRestingOnThePredecessorItRetiresStaysCurrent, and that judging at end-of-log fails TestTwoReceiptsInOneLogAreEachJudgedAtTheirOwnVerdict. Check the four new fixtures are not vacuous. Confirm docs/reference/architecture.md, docs/reference/gs/merge.md, AGENTS.md and SKILL.md still match the code. Rule on whether a before/after fold benchmark is required before approval; I did not take one and am not claiming a number. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification. File approved or changes-requested with gs review naming all seven artifacts. Any head change invalidates review.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}